                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Metamorfose S, is a 2D sci-fi action-adventure game with Metroidvania and RPG elements. Taking control of Sebastian a bioengineered synth experiment created by a scientist named Gerry players are tasked with hunting down and exterminating a rogue species that has united to stage an uprising. Navigating an interconnected map filled with hazardous environments and diverse bio-monsters, you must slice through foes, cast offensive spells, collect crafting loot, and acquire key upgrades to venture deeper into the facility.\n\nThe game’s primary strength lies in its surprisingly deep progression systems and retro aesthetic. Combining traditional Metroidvania backtracking with a full character leveling system, selectable spells, a bestiary, and item crafting allows for considerable character customization. The retro pixel art and atmospheric dark-synth soundtrack create a solid classic-gaming vibe, while responsive controller support ensures that basic movement, spellcasting, and platforming feel fluid during combat encounters.\n\nWhere Metamorfose S experiences friction, however, is in its unpolished level pacing and occasional mechanical stiffness. The map layout features several uninspired corridors with repetitive enemy placements that make backtracking feel tedious rather than rewarding. Furthermore, boss fights can fluctuate wildly in difficulty, with untelegraphed attacks and awkward hitboxes occasionally forcing frustrating trial-and-error deaths that disrupt the overall momentum.\n\nWhile it retains some budget-title rough edges, Metamorfose S delivers a satisfying, nostalgic Metroidvania experience with enough RPG depth and sci-fi atmosphere to merit a recommendation for fans of 2D exploration platformers.\n\nScore: 7/10",
